\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Holy Lamb, who Thee confess,
\par Followers of Thy holiness,
\par Thee they ever keep in view,
\par Ever ask: What shall we do?
\par Governed by Thy only will.
\par All Thy words we would fulfil,
\par Would in all Thy footsteps go.
\par Walk as Jesus walked below.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. While Thou didst on earth appear,
\par Servant to Thy sevants here,
\par Mindful of Thy place above,
\par All Thy life was prayer and love.
\par Such our whole employment be,
\par Works of faith and charity;
\par Works of love on man bestowed,
\par Secret intercourse with God.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Early in the temple met,
\par Let us still our Saviour greet;
\par Nightly to the mount repair,
\par Join our praying Pattern there.
\par There by wresting faith obtain
\par Power to work for God again,
\par Power His image to retrieve,
\par Power, like Thee, our Lord, to live.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Vessels, instruments of grace,
\par Pass we thus our happy days
\par 'Twixt the mount and multitude,
\par Doing or receiving good;
\par Glad to pray and labour on,
\par Till our earthly course is run,
\par Till we, on the sacred tree,
\par Bow the head and die like Thee.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

